messages:
maya: Quick design review — noticed the help CTA in the top-right is visually competing with the small 'Docs' micro-CTA inside the workflow panels. Fig: https://www.figma.com/file/EXAMPLE (see header + panel states)  @jordan

jordan: Saw this in the prototype. Two problems: (1) terminology inconsistency (Docs vs Help vs Documentation) and (2) a11y — VoiceOver reads the header button and then the panel heading redundantly when the sidecar opens.

sam: Confirming the a11y issue. aria-labels aren't harmonized. Current header button = `aria-label="open help"` and panel heading = `role=heading` text "Docs" so screen readers produce duplication.

eli: Also the link behavior is inconsistent — some doc links open a new tab, others route into the console sidecar. That breaks task flow. I think internal anchors should open the sidecar and preserve context.

maya: Proposed small set of changes so we can iterate: 1) unify wording to a single term (docs vs documentation) across header, panels, tooltips; 2) always open internal doc anchors in the sidecar (no new tab); 3) standardize aria-labels like `Open documentation panel` and ensure panel heading is programmatic-only (aria-hidden when redundant). Feedback? :thinking_face:

jordan: My take: prefer the authoritative term "Documentation" (users search for that). It's slightly longer but clear. If UI space is tight, tooltip and aria can use full phrase while visible label stays short — e.g., visible "Docs" with tooltip/aria "Open Documentation panel".

sam: From accessibility POV that pattern works — visible shorthand plus full descriptive aria label. Also add focus management: when sidecar opens, focus should move to the panel heading and focus trap must allow ESC to close.

eli: Tech implementation note: sidecar is routed at `/console/docs?anchor=<id>`. Right now external links use full href and default browser behavior. We can intercept internal doc links and route client-side. Example handler to add to the docs renderer:

```js
function handleDocLinkClick(e) {
  const href = e.target.closest('a')?.href;
  if (!href) return;
  if (isInternalDoc(href)) {
    e.preventDefault();
    const anchor = extractAnchor(href);
    router.push(`/console/docs?anchor=${anchor}`);
    telemetry.track('help.cta.open', { source: currentSource });
  }
}
document.addEventListener('click', handleDocLinkClick);
```

jordan: Love the handler. Add telemetry dimensions: `source=header|panel|in-docs`, `action=open`, `method=keyboard|mouse|shortcut`.

maya: Can we add a keyboard shortcut suggestion? e.g., `Shift?/` to open documentation. Good for power users.

sam: Shortcut OK but needs discoverability and no conflict. Add tooltip text on hover with shortcut and also include an accessible hint: `aria-describedby` to announce the shortcut.

ops-bot: deploy-bot: FYI — planned canary deploy tonight 02:00 UTC for small header copy and telemetry changes.

docs-bot: I pushed a docs redirects PR to preserve old anchors; PR: https://github.com/redwood/console-docs/pull/512 — includes mapping for legacy anchors used in blog posts.

maya: Action items recapped: Jordan — update copy options in Figma and add short/long label proposal (EOD). Eli — implement link intercept + telemetry and add keyboard shortcut support (canary). Sam — add aria-label changes, focus management, and tooltip copy. docs-bot — verify redirects and update anchor mapping. We'll check progress in tomorrow's design sync. Thanks all :thumbsup:
